- (3) Acknowledges full responsibility for complying with the existing privately owned private or public facility permit.

(B) Failure to provide advance notice of a transfer renders the privately owned private or public facility permit void as of the date of the facility transfer.

1.4.5 Same--Revocation.

(A) | The Town Council or its designated agent may revoke a privately owned private or public facility permit for good cause including, but not limited to, the following reasons:

- (1) Failure to notify the Town Council or its designated agent of significant changes to the wastewater prior to the changed discharge;

- (2) Failure to provide prior notification to the Town Council or its designated agent of changed conditions pursuant to 1.5.4 of this Ordinance;

- (3) Misrepresentation or failure to fully disclose all relevant facts in the privately owned private or public facility permit application;

- (4) Falsifying self-monitoring reports; (5) Tampering with monitoring equipment;

- (6) Refusing to allow the Town Council or its designated agent timely access to the facility premises and records;

- (7) Failure to meet effluent limitations; (8) Failure to pay fines;

- (9) Failure to pay sewer charges;

- (10) Failure to meet compliance schedules;

- (11) Failure to complete a wastewater survey or the privately owned private or public facility permit application;

- (12) Failure to provide advance notice of the transfer of business ownership of permitted facility; or

- (13) Violation of any treatment standard or requirement, or any terms of the privately owned private or public facility permit or this Ordinance.

(B) Privately owned private or public facility permits shall be voidable upon cessation of operations or transfer of business ownership. All privately owned private or public facility

